---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Pesticide-Free Cape Town" description="Tools and community support to help Cape Town suburbs move off the City's blanket herbicide spray schedule.">
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>Campaigns</span><span aria-current="page">Pesticide-Free Cape Town</span></nav>
    <p class="eyebrow">Active campaign · Cape Town</p>
    <h1>Pesticide-Free Cape Town</h1>
    <p class="lede">UnPoison is helping communities replace blanket roadside herbicide spraying with safer, non-chemical weed control—and helping residents win exemption from the municipal spray schedule.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href="https://forms.gle/1ms2P4N5C48aebw56">Add your voice <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfnQLLrH1aXaohLnGUWJ4gk3p6BWtwwXb-otIwJQiXNPsP5sA/viewform?usp=header" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Become a suburb champion <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div class="campaign-video">
        <a class="campaign-video-poster" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qc1jjcGwESE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch UnPoison Our City on YouTube (opens in a new tab)">
          <img src="/images/cape-town-1600.webp" width="1600" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <span class="campaign-video-poster-content"><span class="campaign-video-play" aria-hidden="true">▶</span><span>Watch on YouTube<strong>UnPoison Our City</strong></span></span>
        </a>
        <p class="fine-print">UnPoison's film about pesticide use in cities. The video opens on YouTube in a new tab.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-copy article-body">
        <p class="eyebrow">The approach</p>
        <h2>Stop routine spraying. Create safer work.</h2>
        <p>Manual weed removal avoids pesticide exposure, protects urban waterways and biodiversity, and directs public spending toward people and environmental stewardship.</p>
        <p>Noordhoek became Cape Town's first suburb to secure roadside spray exemption in 2023. The campaign now helps more communities organise, document support and follow the City's exemption process.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule campaign-map-band" aria-labelledby="campaign-map-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Suburb status</p><h2 id="campaign-map-title">Where has the spraying changed?</h2></div>
        <p>The community-maintained map from the original campaign page distinguishes suburbs that are sprayed, those with an active champion, partially exempt areas and fully exempt areas.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="campaign-map-preview" href="https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/smnGP/4/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the interactive Cape Town suburb-status map (opens in a new tab)">
        <img src="/images/cape-town-spray-status-map.png" width="1220" height="1856" alt="Map of Cape Town suburbs showing areas still sprayed, areas with an active champion, partially exempt areas and fully exempt areas; the interactive version provides suburb details." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </a>
      <p class="fine-print">Static preview captured 6 October 2026. <a href="https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/smnGP/4/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the live interactive map</a> for suburb details. UnPoison Community Network data is published in beta and may change; check the <a href="https://www.capetown.gov.za/general/weed-spraying-information-and-schedules" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City’s current weed-spraying schedules</a> for official programme information.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Campaign tools</p><h2>Start with the facts.</h2></div>
        <p class="lede">Check the municipal schedule, understand the City's spraying rules and document non-compliance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="action-routes">
        <a class="action-route" href="https://www.capetown.gov.za/general/weed-spraying-information-and-schedules" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="number">CITY</span><span><h3>Current spray schedule and products</h3><p>The City’s changing district schedules, listed herbicides, protocol and complaint route.</p></span><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="action-route" href="/documents/is-this-herbicide-spraying-legal.pdf"><span class="number">PDF</span><span><h3>Is this spraying legal?</h3><p>A practical compliance guide for residents observing municipal spraying.</p></span><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="action-route" href="https://www.capetown.gov.za/general/weed-spraying-information-and-schedules" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="number">CITY</span><span><h3>Report a spraying concern</h3><p>Download the City’s contravention form and follow its submission instructions.</p></span><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="action-route" href="/report-an-incident/"><span class="number">US</span><span><h3>Tell UnPoison what happened</h3><p>Send a first account so we can discuss how your report may support advocacy.</p></span><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="fine-print campaign-archive-link">The original campaign also shared a <a href="/documents/cape-town-herbicide-spraying-information.pdf">City spraying information PDF</a>. Use the City’s live page above for current schedules.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule campaign-join-band" aria-labelledby="campaign-join-title">
    <div class="shell campaign-info-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Work with your neighbours</p><h2 id="campaign-join-title">Become a Suburb Champion.</h2></div>
      <div class="article-body">
        <p>Champions coordinate local support for exemption from the City’s spray schedule. The original campaign describes them liaising with residents, councillors, other champions and UnPoison; organising non-chemical alternatives; and watching for spraying that may not follow the City’s rules.</p>
        <p>UnPoison says it can share tools, templates and a network of people who have already worked through the process. The <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfnQLLrH1aXaohLnGUWJ4gk3p6BWtwwXb-otIwJQiXNPsP5sA/viewform?usp=header" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Champs sign-up form</a> lets you choose suburb work, a thematic focus or both.</p>
        <p>Not ready to coordinate? <a href="https://forms.gle/1ms2P4N5C48aebw56" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Complete the suburb spraying poll</a> to register your view, or <a href="/donate/">support the work financially</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule" aria-labelledby="campaign-faq-title">
    <div class="shell campaign-info-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Campaign questions</p><h2 id="campaign-faq-title">What people ask.</h2></div>
      <div class="article-body animals-faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What does the City spray on roadsides, parks and verges?</summary>
          <div><p>The City lists different products for hard surfaces and for turf areas, with seasonal differences. Its <a href="https://www.capetown.gov.za/general/weed-spraying-information-and-schedules" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">weed-spraying page</a> identifies the products, application details and current district schedules. Check that source rather than relying on an older product list.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is spraying in public areas legal?</summary>
          <div><p>Permitted use is subject to legal requirements and the City’s own operating protocol. UnPoison’s <a href="/documents/is-this-herbicide-spraying-legal.pdf">spraying-compliance guide</a> explains what residents can observe. The <a href="https://www.capetown.gov.za/general/weed-spraying-information-and-schedules" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City publishes its protocol and tender specifications</a>. Whether a particular incident complied depends on its facts; this page is not legal advice.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I report spraying that may breach the rules?</summary>
          <div><p>The City asks residents to complete the weed-spraying contraventions complaint form linked from its <a href="https://www.capetown.gov.za/general/weed-spraying-information-and-schedules" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">spraying information page</a>, then email it and any safe-to-collect evidence to <a href="mailto:contact.us@capetown.gov.za">contact.us@capetown.gov.za</a>. You can also <a href="/report-an-incident/">tell UnPoison</a>; our current first-contact route is email while the previous reporting form is assessed.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How can I help change the spraying programme?</summary>
          <div><p><a href="https://forms.gle/1ms2P4N5C48aebw56" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Add your view to the suburb poll</a> and share it locally. If you can help organise, <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfnQLLrH1aXaohLnGUWJ4gk3p6BWtwwXb-otIwJQiXNPsP5sA/viewform?usp=header" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">join UnPoison Champs</a>. The campaign also welcomes research, data, design, communications and fundraising help; <a href="/contact/">contact the team</a> to offer a skill.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
